      "writtenOn": "2026-05-12T03:26:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@liorsu@google.com,\n\nI think we can simplify the current metrics by:\n1) Keeping nfsv4__op_latency as the source-of-truth metric ( optionally renaming metrics as nfs_op_latency)\n2) Replacing nfs_latency_ms with Prometheus recording rules\n\nBecause, Both(nfsv4__op_latency,nfs_latency_ms) essentially represent the same underlying latency data, but at different abstraction levels.\n\nExample recording rule:\n-----------\ngroups:\n- name: nfs_latency_rules\n  rules:\n  - record: nfs_latency_ms_bucket\n    expr: sum by (le, op) (\n      nfsv4__op_latency_bucket{status\u003d\"NFS4_OK\"}\n    )\n\n  - record: nfs_latency_ms_sum\n    expr: sum by (op) (\n      nfsv4__op_latency_sum{status\u003d\"NFS4_OK\"}\n    )\n\n  - record: nfs_latency_ms_count\n    expr: sum by (op) (\n      nfsv4__op_latency_count{status\u003d\"NFS4_OK\"}\n    )\n-------------\nSO that:\n\n1) Dashboards continue to work (same metric names preserved)\n2) We avoid duplicate instrumentation in code\n3) We keep full fidelity (status-level visibility is still available)",
      "parentUuid": "e8ad3b85_6673609b",
      "revId": "f555be5f7f093ea98dc61720a28e6563ec2a3d05",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
